  <ym-title|Paid response price><label|paid-response-price>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, trace selected-scale producer.

    <item>Status: draft; the native-price identity, ticket calculation, and
    inverse-dilation-to-scaled-root application have been corrected and sent
    for independent review.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-bill-prices.tex>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source crosswalk><label|source-crosswalk>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  statement>>|<cell|<strong|Exact source>>|<cell|<strong|Evidence>>>|<row|<cell|Native
  root allowance and inverse dilation norm>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.nativeC>,
  <verbatim|.alto_norm>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Casa.lean>,
  <verbatim|Annual.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|nativeC> is the stake divided by
  the normalized flight, inverse dilation norm, cubic volume scale, and gain.
  <verbatim|alto_norm> gives the inverse dilation norm
  (A_J^{-d}).>>|<row|<cell|Rate tickets>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.stakeK>,
  <verbatim|.hullK>, <verbatim|.stickK>, <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.grantK>,
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.open_budget>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Fund.lean>, <verbatim|Arms.lean>,
  <verbatim|Stanza.lean>>|<cell|These provide rate-zero tickets for stakes,
  dilation ratio, summit scale, and inverse flight, using basin below summit.
  <verbatim|Ticket.prod> combines them; <verbatim|toll_small> turns the
  product into the <verbatim|Tau(70)> bound.>>|<row|<cell|Gain
  comparison>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.gainsK>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Arms.lean>>|<cell|Gives
  <verbatim|Tau(i,500)\<leq\>gainChart(summit(i),basin(i))>. The product
  identity <verbatim|Tau(70)/Tau(500)=Tau(-430)> yields the rate in the
  manuscript.>>|<row|<cell|Paid label column
  estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Bill>, <verbatim|.majesty>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Casa.lean>,
  <verbatim|Annual.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Bill.norms> and
  <verbatim|Bill.bias>, with threshold at most one and
  <verbatim|AgeK(-1/4)\<leq\>1>, imply the column-size bound 2 by the
  triangle inequality.>>|<row|<cell|Actual label producer
  boundary>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.purchasing>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Casa.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.riches>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Soot/Coffer.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|purchasing>
  converts an atomic paid receipt to a <verbatim|Bill>, using the
  resource-transfer theorem <verbatim|riches>, its <verbatim|SharpRead>
  price-duality input, and finite-volume response receipts. Their production
  remains upstream; the draft currently states this boundary but does not
  prove <verbatim|riches>.>>>>>

